; Run the command check and fetch its result
;
; Calls #R$950F, the check of the command (with ActionPerform, $B6FA, at 0 the
; verb handlers only check and ActionAllowed is set; see #R$9D44), then reads
; ActionAllowed ($B6FB). #R$9D44 sets it to 1 when a check passes and #R$72DD sets
; it to 0 when a message is printed in a check, so 0 here means the command is
; refused (finding F10: the name is inverted).
;
; O:A ActionAllowed ($B6FB)
; O:F Z when it is 0
@label=RunCheck
c$7AED CALL $950F    ;
 $7AF0 LD A,($B6FB)  ;
 $7AF3 AND A         ;
 $7AF4 RET           ;
